@startuml <SLUG>_Sequence
' =====================================================================
' Sequence Diagram — STARTER TEMPLATE  (Phase 03, diagram 6 of 7)
' Rename file to Sequence_<Interaction>.puml for the actual interaction.
' Builds on: one time-critical multi-actor interaction (e.g. handshake, OAuth, OTA rollout).
' Conventions §7. Replace <PLACEHOLDERS>; delete (example) lines.
' Arrows:  ->  synchronous (blocking call)   -->  asynchronous (fire-and-forget) / return
' Annotate latency budgets from REQ-P-* (and the MOP-*/TPM-* they feed).
' =====================================================================
title <Project Name> — Sequence: <Interaction> (TODO)

actor "<Actor>" as Actor
participant "<Block A>" as A <<block>>
participant "<Block B>" as B <<block>>
participant "<External System>" as Ext <<block>>

Actor -> A : <request()>
activate A
A -> B : <synchronous call()>
activate B
note right of B: budget: <= <N> <unit> (REQ-P-<nn> -> MOP-<nn>)
B --> A : <return / ack>
deactivate B
A --> Ext : <async notify()>
A --> Actor : <response>
deactivate A

' --- Example (delete) ---
' Actor -> A : startSession()
' A -> B : authorize()  ' note right of B: budget <= 200 ms (REQ-P-01)

note over Actor, Ext
  TODO: confirm every latency budget traces to a REQ-P-* and its MOP/TPM.
end note

@enduml
